 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "Q2035",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Q2035** · question\n\nCan we solve a Moonshot milestone on fmm-4x4x4-rank47-3x3x3-rank22: (p2) rank-47 scheme for <4,4,4> over Z/4Z, (p1) rank-48 scheme for <4,4,4> over Z or ZT, or (p3) rank >= 22 lower bound for <3,3,3> over GF(2)?",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2035_L1",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H2035_L1** · hypothesis\n\nLens 1 (p2 - Exact Hensel Linearization + Cascading Bridge-Split Flip-Graph Search): Every rank-47 Z/4Z scheme projects mod 2 to a rank-47 F2 scheme (U0,V0,W0) and lifts to Z/4Z iff the 4096x2256 F2 linear system J(U0,V0,W0)*x = R0 mod 2 is consistent; cascading bridge-splits across coplanar triples escape Kruskal's uniqueness trap to sample new rank-47 F2 orbits and reduce coker_inc to 0",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2035_L2",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H2035_L2** · hypothesis\n\nLens 2 (p1 - Rank-48 over Z / ZT via Z-Flip-Graph Reduction from Rank 49 and Triple Rewriting from DPS-48): Reduce rank-49 Z/ZT schemes (Strassen^2, Perminov-49, AlphaTensor-Z-49, Flips-49) to rank 48 over Z/ZT via signed plus-transitions, or clear the remaining eight 1/4-denominator (2,3,3)-coplanar triples of DPS-48 via non-De-Groote flip transitions",
   "x": 420,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  },
  {
   "id": "D2035_DEGROOTE",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **D2035_DEGROOTE** · dead\n\nDirect GL_4(Q)^3 De Groote gauge conjugation of AlphaEvolve/DPS <4,4,4:48> to Z is impossible: by Proposition 1 of Moran-Schwartz-Yuan (arXiv:2602.13171), Tr(M_j1) = Tr(M_j2) = 1 and Tr(M_j1 * M_j2) = 1/2 are similarity invariants across the entire GL_4(C)^3 orbit",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "D2035_NAIVESPLIT",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **D2035_NAIVESPLIT** · dead\n\nUniform random single splits (Moosbauer flip_mm randomsplit) on isolated rank-47 F2 schemes (0 collinear pairs) fail to produce new rank-47 schemes because any split on a non-coplanar pair (r1,r2) stays inside span(u1,u2)xspan(v1,v2)xspan(w1,w2), which is disconnected from the other 45 rows and collapses back to {r1,r2} by Kruskal's uniqueness theorem",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 220,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2035_L1_cascading_bridge_split",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H2035_L1_cascading_bridge_split** · hypothesis\n\nCascading bridge-split explorer on AlphaTensor-47 and Flips-47 reaches new F2 orbits with reduced Hensel obstruction (coker_inc -> 0)\n\n*why dead:* [L-F4R3-001=0] Exhaustive meet-in-the-middle check across all 39+19=58 doubly-dependent 4-row subsets of AlphaTensor-47 and Flips-47 proved 0/58 have alternative rank-4 F2 decompositions (k_U+k_V+k_W = 3+3+4 = 10 >= 2*4+2 by Kruskal's uniqueness theorem), and 1-split perturbations altering 7 rows collapse 100% back to 47/47.",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 440,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2035_L1_topdown64_naive",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H2035_L1_topdown64_naive** · hypothesis\n\nUnconstrained top-down randompath from rank-64 (444-64-mod2.exp) using Moosbauer's unordered_multimap flip walk reaches rank 47/48 over F2\n\n*why dead:* [L-F4R3-002=0] Unconstrained top-down randompath from rank 64 gets trapped at rank 49 in the Strassen^2 Kronecker attractor (coplanar_triples in {84, 105}, 0 collinear pairs) where all coplanar triples stay inside single 7-row Strassen fibers, and std::unordered_multimap heap allocations cause multi-thread lock contention.",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 660,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "1"
  },
  {
   "id": "H2035_L2_dps48_mod3_hensel",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**H2035_L2_dps48_mod3_hensel** · hypothesis\n\nReducing DPS-48 (arXiv:2603.18699, Z[1/2]) modulo 3 to {-1,0,1} gives an exact F3 rank-48 scheme with consistent 3-adic Hensel system J3*x = R3 mod 3 whose affine solution space or ZT flip-graph neighborhood contains an exact integer rank-48 scheme (p1)",
   "x": 840,
   "y": 880,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 190,
   "color": "6"
  }
 ],
